{"shortDescription":"Banks including Goldman Sachs and Bank of America NYSE:BAC have raised their oil price forecasts this week as persistent disruptions to Middle East shipping tightened oil markets and drove crude prices to multi-week highs.","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Banks including Goldman Sachs and Bank of America ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYSE:BAC","text":"NYSE:BAC"}}," have raised their oil price forecasts this week as persistent disruptions to ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/iran/","linkText":"Middle East"}}," shipping tightened oil markets and drove crude prices to multi-week highs."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Goldman Sachs on Monday raised its Brent and West Texas Intermediate crude oil price forecasts by $5 a barrel for December 2026 and 2027, citing an expectation that shipping disruptions in the Middle East will persist into next year."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The bank in a note said that Brent crude could climb above $120 a barrel if average Gulf oil output in 2027 remains 4 million barrels per day below pre-war levels, compared with its base case assumption of a 0.5 million bpd shortfall."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["It also noted that Brent crude could fall into the $60s in 2027 under a downside price scenario in which average Gulf oil output rises 1 million bpd above pre-war levels."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["HSBC on Tuesday raised its 2026 and 2027 Brent price forecasts to $90 and $85 a barrel, respectively."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"We think the market is adjusting to a disrupted 'new normal' in which the strait is neither fully closed nor fully open, but persistently impaired,\" HSBC said in a note, referring to the Strait of Hormuz shipping route."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["